@model bool
@* The resident's self-serve <b>change-password</b> section (ADR 0138),
   co-located with MFA on the Security tab (moved from its own
   /account/password tab 2026-10-31 — "one tab, both credential-security
   options"). Rendered by both the Mfa.cshtml and MfaLocked.cshtml views
   (so a resident who is MFA-locked but not password-locked still keeps
   their change-password lane, and vice-versa). The model is the
   PasswordChangeLocked flag (the ADR 0138 four-conjunct decision, the
   SecuritySettingsController.IsPasswordChangeLockedAsync read):
     @Model == true  → the "password changes are locked" notice (a non-admin
                       sample account on an opted-in demo instance);
     @Model == false → the change-password form (the floor, and every real /
                       non-sample account).
   The write lane is POST /settings/security/password (the
   SecuritySettingsController.ChangePassword action — the ADR 0138 self-serve
   guard, the single audited identity.ChangePasswordAsync write lane). The form
   mirrors the original Views/Account/ChangePassword.cshtml field-for-field (the
   three password fields + the kw-l keys, all already registered in the
   KnownTranslationKeys registry). The action URL is a literal (the same
   convention as the adjacent MFA forms — this controller uses attribute
   routing, so asp-action would not resolve). *@

@* ── Locked notice (the ADR 0138 "surface replaced by a notice" shape) ── *@
@if (Model)
{
    <h2 class="mt-4"><kw-l key="account.change_password_title">Change password</kw-l></h2>
    <div class="alert alert-info">
        <kw-l key="account.change_password_locked_title">Password changes are locked</kw-l>
        <div class="mt-2 text-muted">
            <kw-l key="account.change_password_locked_body">This is a demo account and password changes are locked by the administrator so everyone can keep using the shared credentials. You can still use every other feature of the platform.</kw-l>
        </div>
    </div>
}
else
{
    <h2 class="mt-4"><kw-l key="account.change_password_title">Change password</kw-l></h2>
    <p class="text-muted">
        <kw-l key="account.change_password_lede">Pick a new password for your account. After saving you'll be signed out and asked to sign in again with the new password.</kw-l>
    </p>

    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body">
            <form method="post" action="/settings/security/password">
                @Html.AntiForgeryToken()

                <div class="mb-3">
                    <label for="CurrentPassword" class="form-label"><kw-l key="account.change_password_current">Current password</kw-l></label>
                    <input type="password" class="form-control" id="CurrentPassword" name="CurrentPassword" autocomplete="current-password" />
                </div>

                <div class="mb-3">
                    <label for="NewPassword" class="form-label"><kw-l key="account.change_password_new">New password</kw-l></label>
                    <input type="password" class="form-control" id="NewPassword" name="NewPassword" autocomplete="new-password" />
                </div>

                <div class="mb-3">
                    <label for="ConfirmNewPassword" class="form-label"><kw-l key="account.change_password_confirm_new">Confirm new password</kw-l></label>
                    <input type="password" class="form-control" id="ConfirmNewPassword" name="ConfirmNewPassword" autocomplete="new-password" />
                </div>

                <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary"><kw-l key="account.change_password_submit">Change password</kw-l></button>
            </form>
        </div>
    </div>
}
